{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1344160-what-can-a-mage-with-arete-10-and-all-spheres-at-5-do","id":1344160,"title":"What can a mage with arete 10 and all spheres at 5 do?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-28T03:35:41-07:00","id":1344160,"title":"What can a mage with arete 10 and all spheres at 5 do?","content":"I have tried getting into mage many times and I am now retrying since from what i have heard M20 streamlines and clears up certain things that always plagued the line.<br /> I though it would be fun to ask this in the forums, since I am a sucker for supernatural powers and from browsing in the forums I thought there certain very interesting stuff mages can do and I like how with imagination you can cut corners to achieve what you want to achieve. <br /> <br /> Only the books published for M20, so no arch spheres allowed. <br /> <br /> Dont answer the question is &quot;What can he not do&quot;(though I do admit its likely the correct answer). If that's the case what would YOU do in WoD? What could successfully at least oppose your mage, that's not another mage?<br /> <br /> If you still find my question just too silly, would the answer change if the arete was 5? What about about if the mage &quot;only&quot; had 500 xp or 1000 xp? <br /> <br /> Pick any focus/paradim/nature etc and whatever level of abilities you like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2024-malfi","name":"Malfi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T04:29:11-07:00","id":1344165,"title":"","content":"Oh that's easy....Anything","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T06:08:03-07:00","id":1344175,"title":"","content":"I have created a thread about what mages cannot do. There you wilk find some answers.<br /> <br /> It is easier to ask what they can't, since they can do almost everything.<br /> <br /> I don't know if the mage could break Caine curse, for example. Or increase Arete","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T06:54:59-07:00","id":1344181,"title":"","content":"I think the point of Malfi is that they didn't want 'everything' as an answer, but a thread with random crazy ideas of things you can see Archmages doing <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Think of it as &quot;<i>1001 things to do with full level 5 spheres</i>&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T14:13:39-07:00","id":1344253,"title":"","content":"Anything in <i>Theor</i>y, but in practice you are limited to your Paradigm. Which is a crappy answer. You can raise the dead, destroy a city or more, rewrite history, create an alternate reality, explore the universe, control the world, and more. It is not a question of where you are going to stop, but who is going to stop you? Power in games does not intimidate me. I like to play with the consequences of power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T15:49:58-07:00","id":1344280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1344160-what-can-a-mage-with-arete-10-and-all-spheres-at-5-do?p=1344181#post1344181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the point of Malfi is that they didn't want 'everything' as an answer, but a thread with random crazy ideas of things you can see Archmages doing <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Think of it as &quot;<i>1001 things to do with full level 5 spheres</i>&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah exactly and I would like to see the details of how you do it. As I said pick a focus an go crazy. If it seems to overwhelming go with arete 5, if it stills seems too much go with 1000xp, if it still seems too much go with 500xp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2024-malfi","name":"Malfi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T18:38:05-07:00","id":1344315,"title":"","content":"Given enough time and what resources they have available would be the ultimate limitation. A master with a number of powerful nodes could make a Horizon Realm for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T18:57:23-07:00","id":1344318,"title":"","content":"Go backwards in time all the way and say &quot;Let there be light!&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T22:44:02-07:00","id":1344352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marko Markoko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1344160-what-can-a-mage-with-arete-10-and-all-spheres-at-5-do?p=1344253#post1344253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anything in <i>Theor</i>y, but in practice you are limited to your Paradigm. Which is a crappy answer. You can raise the dead, destroy a city or more, rewrite history, create an alternate reality, explore the universe, control the world, and more. It is not a question of where you are going to stop, but who is going to stop you? Power in games does not intimidate me. I like to play with the consequences of power.</div> </div> </div> </div>At ten Arete you have ZERO instruments, meaning your paradigm is probably /extremely/ fucking vague and open right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-29T04:42:59-07:00","id":1344385,"title":"","content":"create worlds, make new sapient species with souls who could become mages, you could transform a single snowflake into a city, make metal interwoven perfectly with candycane at the molecular level which is enchanted so that anyone who eats it turns into teletubbies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-29T11:53:35-07:00","id":1344461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jihelu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1344160-what-can-a-mage-with-arete-10-and-all-spheres-at-5-do?p=1344352#post1344352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At ten Arete you have ZERO instruments, meaning your paradigm is probably /extremely/ fucking vague and open right now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I figure that at this point, it has become very well defined. That is why you don't need Instruments. But if you are trying to pull of some mega feat, you will probably use them anyway. And you will probably be using a Ritual.<br /> <br /> It isn't <i>what</i> you do, but<i> how</i> that is guided by Paradigm. For example, Creating a Dragon. A Progenitor would grow the monster in a lab. Or even if not using Instruments, she would use her &quot;power&quot; to write upon reality a DNA sequence that would &quot;mimic&quot; a dragon-like monster that fits her understanding of science. But she could never fathom how a Hermetic Archmagus does the same thing. He seeks out the cave of a dragon of legend, whispers in Enochian to call out to its spirit, coaxes it to return to reality and weaves flesh from magic with the dragon's guidance. Or an Akashic Mage uses some Dragonballs. Even without these Instruments, in their hearts and minds, they are bringing a Bygone into the modern age. They are not growing it out of thin air using a DNA design in their head.<br /> <br /> Doctor Manhattan would just weave spontaneously generated particles into the desired form.To him, Spirit is a creation if the Mind which is a natural function of Life. A Hermetic may think it goes Mind, Life, Spirit. Verbenae think it goes Life, Spirit, Mind. The Akashic way is Spirit, Life, Mind. The end results are (mostly) the same. The difference is in what the Mage is thinking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-29T12:42:02-07:00","id":1344478,"title":"","content":"I figure at Arete 10 I'm mainly focused on Ascending.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-29T13:55:27-07:00","id":1344495,"title":"","content":"The progenitor example isn't all that good because M20 hates the Technocracy and they never lose instruments, ever. The mightiest Proginiter is still using a cloning lab to make dragons. Quite literally the Hermetic could do it without words, he doesn't need to whisper, he just needs to will it in the world. Words make it slightly easier with a -1 DC.<br /> <br /> At this point they are also on the cusp of ascending, if they haven't already become an oracle. I think M20 even defines 10 arete as awakening/oracle status (Which brings the weird edition bias into the mix as editions have heavily changed their opinion on whether or not Oracles are demi gods, if awakening is just hitting 10 arete, and so on). They are about to transcend reality and relying on their old tools are the things that keep them tied down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-29T18:02:11-07:00","id":1344542,"title":"","content":"Technocrats transcend all of their Instruments at once when they reach an Arete of 10.<br /> And if it is time to Ascend, I am taking my dragon with me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-29T20:57:32-07:00","id":1344570,"title":"","content":"No, they do not.<br /> <br /> &quot;Technocrats receive so much indoctrination that they never break through their preconceptions that way. Unless he leaves the Technocracy to pursue a different Path, a Technocrat remains convinced that his faction\u2019s perception of reality is the only one that truly works\u2026 and that perspective <b>demands instruments of science</b>, even if those instruments aren\u2019t always obvious. At Arete 10, a Technocrat becomes part of the Machine \u2013 a focus for the Will of technology instead of the other way around.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Even if those instruments aren't always obvious&quot; could lead to some real stupid and crazy acts of science shittery, but their paradigm demands science + tools.<br /> <br /> Though I guess this means I could throw my body against the wall and quantum physics says there's a chance I go flying through it and teleport through the wall, so it seems to happen.<br /> <br /> And I get the dragon, I named him and everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-29T22:25:44-07:00","id":1344586,"title":"","content":"I challenge thee Certamen! Rego!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T11:24:10-07:00","id":1344997,"title":"","content":"Thanks for answering! Some good stuff, but maybe my initial question was too broad.<br /> How about I change it to &quot;Go ahead what would you do if you were a mage with 1000 xp in wod?&quot;<br /> For consistency's sake use all the non optional rules from the core rulebook. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2024-malfi","name":"Malfi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-03T10:09:51-08:00","id":1345605,"title":"","content":"With Mind5/Life5/Corr5 you could simultaneously split yourself across several duplicates and do a lot more per day than with just one body/mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-03T12:04:55-08:00","id":1345618,"title":"","content":"I think Life 5 says you you can do this with just Life 5 (In HDYDT if you are using M20), and I think it suggests being able to do this otherwise with Life 4/Correspondence 4/Mind 1. There are some rules on what happens if one of you dies though.<br /> <br /> Also Life 5 lets you turn yourself into like 3 tigers and 2 lions. It's great","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T01:02:11-08:00","id":1345725,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't that cause paradox?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2024-malfi","name":"Malfi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T04:36:53-08:00","id":1345753,"title":"","content":"With Arete 10 and Prime 5 you don't mind much about paradox...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T13:01:19-08:00","id":1345859,"title":"","content":"I have become Death, the Destroyer of Worlds...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T14:41:13-08:00","id":1345903,"title":"","content":"Yes it causes paradox but heres the thing:<br /> <br /> Everything you do, barring TIME and only if you use HDYDT, only incurs 1 point of paradox per vulgar casting. Assuming you don't botch and ST fiat. This isn't to say this is a /bad/ thing, I think if you nuke a major city you should get some hefty paradox, but here's the thing.<br /> <br /> LIttle Jimmy the Mage does a Force 2 jedi push, and gets 1 Paradox because he succeeded.<br /> <br /> Little Jimmy is now big Jimmy and uses Forces 5 to turn an entire area around him into a hellish nuclear wasteland that quickly dissipates into quintessence by using the addition of Prime, vaporizing everything around himself.<br /> He gets 1 Paradox because he succeeded and a shit ton of quintessence. Next turn he uses Prime 5 to get rid of paradox by using Quintessence.<br /> <br /> It really doesn't matter all that much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T10:07:50-08:00","id":1350663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marko Markoko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1344160-what-can-a-mage-with-arete-10-and-all-spheres-at-5-do?p=1344542#post1344542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technocrats transcend all of their Instruments at once when they reach an Arete of 10.<br /> And if it is time to Ascend, I am taking my dragon with me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ascension is only loosely related to Arete. Plus Arete 10 is supposed to be ridiculously rare in the lore. As in, it's doubtful if any of them has that much<br /> <br /> That's why the &quot;transcend their instruments with arete 10&quot; is a very stupid rule indeed. ALL higher ranking technocrats know they are reality warpers. They just pretend. They should start transcending instruments at arete 6 imo","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T10:07:50-08:00","id":1350664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marko Markoko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1344160-what-can-a-mage-with-arete-10-and-all-spheres-at-5-do?p=1344542#post1344542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technocrats transcend all of their Instruments at once when they reach an Arete of 10.<br /> And if it is time to Ascend, I am taking my dragon with me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ascension is only loosely related to Arete. Plus Arete 10 is supposed to be ridiculously rare in the lore. As in, it's doubtful if any of them has that much<br /> <br /> That's why the &quot;transcend their instruments with arete 10&quot; is a very stupid rule indeed. ALL higher ranking technocrats know they are reality warpers. They just pretend. They should start transcending instruments at arete 6 imo","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-04T11:00:40-08:00","id":1352644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jihelu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1344160-what-can-a-mage-with-arete-10-and-all-spheres-at-5-do?p=1345903#post1345903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes it causes paradox but heres the thing:<br /> <br /> Everything you do, barring TIME and only if you use HDYDT, only incurs 1 point of paradox per vulgar casting. Assuming you don't botch and ST fiat. This isn't to say this is a /bad/ thing, I think if you nuke a major city you should get some hefty paradox, but here's the thing.<br /> <br /> LIttle Jimmy the Mage does a Force 2 jedi push, and gets 1 Paradox because he succeeded.<br /> <br /> Little Jimmy is now big Jimmy and uses Forces 5 to turn an entire area around him into a hellish nuclear wasteland that quickly dissipates into quintessence by using the addition of Prime, vaporizing everything around himself.<br /> He gets 1 Paradox because he succeeded and a shit ton of quintessence. Next turn he uses Prime 5 to get rid of paradox by using Quintessence.<br /> <br /> It really doesn't matter all that much.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What about spells with duration or hanged spells?<br /> For spells with duration you can have some constantly vulgar things going on. With time 3 you could have the mage constantly taking 20 actions per round for 6 months. Wouldn't you incur paradox everytime you use more than the 3 action limit described in hydt?<br /> I know raising physical attributes is prohibitive, but still I am sure you could find very powerful effects to layer on mage that are clearly vulgar and will last more than your 1 point of paradox.<br /> Simiralry for hanged spells, if you hang a spell (with time 4/entropy 3?) you take the paradox when you trigger it or when you release it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2024,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2024-malfi","user":"Malfi","date":". 12-04-2019, 02:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2024-malfi","name":"Malfi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-04T16:24:25-08:00","id":1352694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jihelu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1344160-what-can-a-mage-with-arete-10-and-all-spheres-at-5-do?p=1344495#post1344495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The progenitor example isn't all that good because M20 hates the Technocracy and they never lose instruments, ever.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say that M20 hates the Technocracy: while they can't ever discard their Instruments, they are compensated for that by being able to mass-produce Devices and Principiae (with proper Technocratic facilities, they can make these Wonders without having to expend Willpower or personal Quintessence; only the Quintessence that gets incorporated into the Wonder). And as I interpret the rules, while Technocrats never Surpass their Instruments, they still get the same difficulty reduction that a more traditional mage gets for using an Instrument that he doesn't need anymore; just without the option of not using it instead: instead of surpassing the instrument, he has mastered it. That takes some of the edge off of the \u201cno Surpassing Instruments\u201d restriction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 12-05-2019, 04:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}